roject's import-linter layers put compare and viz as independent siblings ('(rllab.train) | (rllab.reference) | (rllab.compare) | (rllab.viz) | (rllab.baselines)'). Writing the frozen signature needs 'from rllab.viz import Chart' in rllab.compare, which fails lint-imports (CR-24) even under TYPE_CHECKING, so the interface cannot pass the gate as specified. Options: (a) let compare depend on viz (architecture + build-setup: layers and the 'compare -> evaluate' rule), (b) move viz.Chart to a lower component (e.g. runs or evaluate) so both can import it, or (c) have run_claims take chart paths (charts: Sequence[Path]). Related nits found while reading: envs.Snake.reset_to returns a bare np.ndarray and dict[str, int] while core.Env.reset returns team-keyed dict obs and dict[str, float] (AD-13); CONSTRAINTS says viz -> runs while pyproject names viz -> runs, evaluate (plot_curves takes evaluate.ScoreSet); and PL-04's load_report_spec/score_players/open_curve_runs pass a 'targets' value (players, baselines, ladder and ablation groups, crossplay charts) and a curves value (.ladder, .ablations) that have no contract type, though they cross tasks M1-T09 and M1-T10.", "type": "compare.run_claims"}
